// "[subject] discards N" ([CR#701.9a]): the DECLARATIVE-SUBJECT discard —
// that player chooses N cards from their hand and discards them
// ([CR#701.9b]). The keyword action as DATA, `Mills`'s twin on the discard
// lane: a `Composite` whose tag is `Discard` and whose body is an ordinary
// `With(Choose(..InHand(who)..), ..)` decision, `who` also naming the
// chooser ([CR#701.9b]'s affected-player default). The engine surfaces the
// choice up front (a `ChooseObjects` decision) and realizes N per-card
// `Act(Discard)` events (madness bites per card, [CR#702.35a]; discard
// triggers fire once per card).
//
// `who` (Param(0)) rides BOTH the atom and the `Choose` binder's `filter`/
// `by`. The template renders the subject context-aware ("Target player
// discards a card."; "Each opponent discards two cards.").
//
// Usage: Discards(It, 1) (the announced player target) / Discards(It, 2).
(
    name: "Discards",
    template: "${0} discards ${1:card|cards}",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect, KeywordAction],
    params: [Reference, Count],
    body: Composite(
        name: Discard,
        body: With(
            binder: Choose(quantity: Exactly(Param(1)), filter: InHand(Param(0)), by: Param(0)),
            body: Each(
                binder: Existing(They),
                effect: Composite(name: Discard, body: Move(It, Graveyard)),
            ),
        ),
    ),
)
